1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.somme.com/en/company/history
2 CONT
2 CONT A family business that started up in bilbao more than one hundred YEARS AGO
2 CONT
2 CONT FOUR GENERATIONS OF SOMMES MANUFACTURING CAN SEAMERS THE EARLY YEARS
2 CONT
2 CONT Johannes Kielland
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1891, the Norwegian Johannes Kielland Somme (a relative of the novelist Alexander Kielland) and his wife Anna Petersen arrived in Spain from the city of Stavanger.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johannes had been hired by the Norwegian timber company Sorensen Yakhelln & Cia ("La Compañía de Maderas") which was founded in 1874 and had offices in several Spanish cities. In 1904, he was made manager of the Bilbao office. Its
2 CONC  central warehouses were located on the site now occupied by the Guggenheim museum.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Eksamen fra Christiania handelsgymnas 1887, deretter to år hos bankierfirma der. 1891 ansatt i det norsk-spanske eksportfirmaet "Compania de Maderas". Oppholdt seg i flere spanske byer inntil han 1904 ble sjef for firmaets filial 
2 CONC i Bilbao. Startet eget firma der 1905 (maskinforretning, mekanisk verksted og gummieringsfabrikk). Norsk generalkonsul i Bilbao 1906.  Kommandør av St. Olavs orden.
